  "source_text": "Good morning. Can I help you? Good morning. I booked a seat on the eight thirty bus to Hillford, but my name isn't on the list at the gate. Let me check. What's the name on the reservation? Maya. I booked it online two days ago. I've found it, but it's for tomorrow, not today. Oh no! I think I chose the wrong date. I really need to travel today. I have a meeting in Hillford at one. That's okay. There are still seats on the eight thirty today. I can change your reservation, but there's a five-dollar fee. How long is the journey? Will I arrive before one? Yes. It takes about three hours, so you'll arrive at about eleven thirty. Great. Then please change it. Can I pay by card? Of course. That's five dollars, please. Thank you. Today's eight thirty bus, seat twelve. Please go to gate three. Today at eight thirty, seat twelve, gate three. Thank you so much!",
